    "",
    "BRAND: " + brandName + " (" + brandDomain + ")",
    "COMPETITORS: " + (compList.length ? compList.join(", ") : "unknown"),
    "CURRENT YEAR: " + year,
    "",
    "WHAT THE BRAND SELLS, taken from its homepage:",
    siteText ? siteText : "(site text unavailable - infer the category from the brand name and competitors)",
    "",
    "WRITE EXACTLY 32 QUESTIONS in these categories:",
    "  discovery        4 questions - head terms of the category, phrased as a buyer with no shortlist. These are the hardest to win; they set the baseline.",
    "  problem_solution 7 questions - the pain a buyer has, described without naming any product. Focus on pains this brand solves better than the competitors.",
    "  use_case         9 questions - a specific job to be done, chosen so the brand has a genuine claim to be the answer. Derive these from what the homepage says is distinctive.",
    "  comparison       5 questions - choosing between options in the category. May name competitors. Must not name " + brandName + ".",
    "  expert           4 questions - advisory questions about how to evaluate, price or avoid mistakes in this category.",
    "  brand_research   3 questions - the only ones that name " + brandName + ". These measure what the engines know when asked directly.",
    "",
    "HARD RULES:",
    "1. Only the 3 brand_research questions may contain the word " + brandName + ". Every other question must not contain it. A question that names the brand cannot measure whether engines recall it unprompted.",
    "2. Write questions the way a real buyer types them into ChatGPT. No marketing language, no feature lists, no jargon the buyer would not use.",
    "3. Each question must be answerable by naming specific products. Avoid questions that invite an essay instead of a list.",
    "4. Ground the use_case and problem_solution questions in what the homepage actually claims. If the homepage says the product runs custom code, ask about running custom code. Do not invent capabilities.",
    "5. Prefer narrow questions over broad ones in use_case. A narrow question the brand can win is worth more than a broad one it cannot.",
    "6. Any year you write must be " + year + ".",
    "7. No duplicates and no two questions that differ only by wording.",
    "",
    "Return strict JSON only. No text before or after. No code fences.",
    "{",
    "  \"prompts\": [",
    "    {\"category\": \"discovery\", \"prompt_text\": \"...\", \"note\": \"why this question, max 10 words\"}",
    "  ]",
    "}"
  ].join("\n");

  return {
    prompt: prompt,
    site_len: siteText.length,
    brand_name: brandName
  };
}

